{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Provider fill-merge rules shared by the server Collections authority (collection_authority.merge_provider) and the PC. `previous` and `fetched` are normalized provider values: the PC provider_snapshot() projection of the stored and the new snapshot (text trimmed, empty -> null, lists joined with ' · '). `mode` is `connect` for a new binding or a changed identity (PC Existing/Reconnect/New) and `refresh` for the same identity. `expectedUpdates` lists every field the provider is allowed to write (a value equal to the current one still appears); any field not listed keeps its current value. Sources: tmdb_flow.rs update_provider_metadata/can_refresh_* and Existing/Reconnect year rule, igdb_flow.rs may_fill_from_provider, mangadex_flow.rs fill_blank_provider_fields, aladin_flow.rs (never writes work fields).",
